  "worked_solution": "From the picture, the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,-2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(1,4),$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{\u2015}{AB},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\u2015}{AB}| & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-3)^{2}+(4-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
